<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">6 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 6 September, from 394 to 1966.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/394">394 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,632 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Theodosius I defeats Eugenius at the Frigidus</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Emperor Theodosius defeated the usurper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eugenius">Eugenius</a>, backed by the pagan senatorial aristocracy, in a two-day battle in the Julian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a>. Traditional Roman religion lost its last political champion.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodosius-i">Theodosius I</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1492">1492 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">534 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Columbus sails from La Gomera on his first Atlantic voyage</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Christopher Columbus</a> left San Sebastián de La Gomera in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canary-islands">Canary Islands</a> on his first expedition across the Atlantic, bound for what he thought were the Indies. His voyages began the Spanish colonisation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Christopher Columbus</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canary-islands">Canary Islands</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1522">1522 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">504 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Victoria completes the first voyage around the world</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Victoria, last survivor of Magellan's five ships, reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> under Juan Sebastián Elcano with 18 men. The voyage revealed the vast size of the Pacific and the true scale of the globe.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1628">1628 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">398 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John Endecott's Puritans arrive at Salem</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-endecott">John Endecott</a> landed at Naumkeag with Puritan settlers, taking charge of the small settlement soon renamed Salem. It became the first town of the Massachusetts Bay Colony.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1634 CE <span class="tih-ago">392 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Imperial and Spanish armies crush the Swedes at Nördlingen</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War, imperial and Spanish forces under the future Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-iii-holy-roman-emperor">Ferdinand III</a> and the Cardinal-Infante Ferdinand crushed the Swedes and their German allies under Gustav Horn and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bernhard-of-saxe-weimar">Bernhard of Saxe-Weimar</a>. The defeat broke Swedish power in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-nordlingen-1634">Battle of Nördlingen</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-years-war">Thirty Years' War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1781">1781 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">245 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Benedict Arnold leads British forces to victory at Groton Heights</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">British forces under Brigadier General Benedict Arnold and Lieutenant Colonel Edmund Eyre defeated a small <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/connecticut">Connecticut</a> militia force led by Lieutenant Colonel William Ledyard. Arnold, once an American major general, had defected to the British in 1780.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolutionary-war">American Revolutionary War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1901">1901 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">125 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">President McKinley is shot in Buffalo</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Anarchist Leon Czolgosz shot <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-mckinley">William McKinley</a> twice at the Pan-American Exposition. The president died eight days later, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodore-roosevelt">Theodore Roosevelt</a> succeeded him.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1966">1966 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">60 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hendrik Verwoerd is stabbed to death in parliament</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>'s prime minister, chief architect of apartheid, was killed in the House of Assembly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-town">Cape Town</a> by parliamentary messenger Dimitri Tsafendas. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apartheid">Apartheid</a> continued under his successors.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 6 September <span class="n">4</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/emir-abdelkader"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/emir-abdelkader.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Emir Abdelkader</span><span class="tp">1808–1883</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/george-etienne-cartier"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/george-etienne-cartier.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">George-Étienne Cartier</span><span class="tp">1814–1873</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/luis-federico-leloir"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/luis-federico-leloir.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Luis Federico Leloir</span><span class="tp">1906–1987</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/peter-ii-of-yugoslavia"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/peter-ii-of-yugoslavia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Peter II of Yugoslavia</span><span class="tp">1923–1970</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 6 September <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/eugenius"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/eugenius.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Eugenius</span><span class="tp">d. 394</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizu-of-liao"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Emperor Taizu of Liao</span><span class="tp">872–926</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/hendrik-verwoerd"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/hendrik-verwoerd.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Hendrik Verwoerd</span><span class="tp">1901–1966</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/eugenia-charles"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/eugenia-charles.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Eugenia Charles</span><span class="tp">1919–2005</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/robert-mugabe"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/robert-mugabe.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Robert Mugabe</span><span class="tp">1924–2019</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
